-- title:
--   Frobenius squared equals the diamond ⟨ p⟩⁻¹ at supersingular places
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M\ge 1$ with $p\mid M$ but $p^2\nmid M$, and a subgroup $H\le(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose reduction in $(\mathbb Z/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$; assume the $q$-expansion $j$-series `jqModC` $\mathbb Q$ lies in the function field $\mathbb Q$-generated by the integral form ratios at full level $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z)$, and let $\mathfrak X$ be a model datum `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and let $\rho\colon R_p\to A$ be a ring homomorphism compatible with the structure map $R_p\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Assume the hypothesis `hdia0`: for every $e\in(\mathbb Z/(M/p))^\times$ and every closed point $P$ of the curve $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{Mfib}$ attached to $(A,\rho)$, the image of $P$ under the special fibre of the level-$(M/p)$ diamond isomorphism $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{dia0}\,e$ (transported along $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{efib}$ and its inverse, the fibre being taken along $\mathrm{residue}_A\circ\rho$) is again a closed point, and its associated place is the translate of the place of $P$ by the semilinear automorphism induced by the $K$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{diamondActionModL}$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ at level $M/p$ with subgroup the image of $H$, evaluated at the chosen lift [`CuspForm.gammaLift (M / p) e`](def/CuspForm_HeckeOperatorFormsGammaH.html#L36) $\in\Gamma_0(M/p)$. Then for every $e$ with $e\cdot p=1$ in $\mathbb Z/(M/p)$ and every place $y$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_N(p,M,H)$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ lying in `ssPlacesQExp` at $p$ (the supersingular places), applying twice the Frobenius operation on places — restriction along the integral map $\mathrm{qExpFrobeniusModL}$, $q\mapsto q^p$ — returns the translate of $y$ by that same diamond semilinear automorphism attached to $e$.
--
--   This is the classical relation $\mathrm{Frob}^2=\langle p\rangle^{-1}$ on the supersingular points of the characteristic-$p$ fibre of a modular curve of level divisible exactly once by $p$, here read off a Deligne–Rapoport-style model through the $q$-expansion function field. It feeds the equivalence [`ModularCurve.diamondActionModL_smul_mem_ssPlacesQExp_iff_and_qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL_qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL_eq_smul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.diamondActionModL_smul_mem_ssPlacesQExp_iff_and_qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL_qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL_eq_smul), part of the analysis of the special fibre used in level lowering at $p$.
-- source:
